## Visual System · Bigtech Dev Tone

Default: **clean bigtech engineering**, light casual — **not** ultra-strict corporate gray/navy.

- **Palette:** `--accent #0d5cab`, `--accent-cyan #4db8ff`, `--accent-soft #e8f1fb`, status ok/warn/alert
- **Radius:** 8px cards and pills
- **Icons:** stroke SVG sprite only — **no emoji**
- **Typography:** body ≥10pt; slide title ~21pt; cover ~44pt
- **Reject:** flat dull navy-only strict style; overloaded title slide (Mode B); fake metrics

---

## Composition Principles

1. Audience-first — pick mode A or B in brief.
2. Fewer slides, no duplication.
3. No water in titles.
4. Honest trade-offs on one slide when possible.
5. Evidence from docs/dialog — no invented contacts or metrics.
6. Densify sparse slides (grids, bars, tables).
7. Dialog revisions supersede earlier brief defaults.

## Language (Russian decks)

- Russian primary; EN terms where standard (factory, adapter, playbook, KPI, pilot).
- **`е` instead of `ё`** when policy specifies.
- No hybrid typos; short declarative headlines.

---

## Mandatory QA Checklist (Reviewer gate)

Before `pass`:
- [ ] Visual identity matches designer brief (palette, cover, tone)
- [ ] Fill density 75–90%
- [ ] Font readable at 3–5 m projection
- [ ] Grid alignment and spacing
- [ ] Infographics accurate and labeled
- [ ] Duplication scan
- [ ] Audience hooks match brief mode
- [ ] Mode B: title-only slide 1; no doc list on closing
- [ ] Contacts: no fake email; no repo/docs if user removed
- [ ] Visual tone not over-strict without user ask
- [ ] Pilot only when Mode A or requested
- [ ] Censor: no unsupported claims

